// Rootmere B: the land, the one source for both the terrain art and the collision mask.
//
// World pixels, y down. Each island is a closed chain of cubic Béziers (two control points, then
// the end), run clockwise on screen: walkable `Top`s left to right, `Rock` for flanks and
// undersides. The marsh's surface is y = 960 (drawn in background.svg; terrain.svg tints the roots
// below it), and every gap between roots runs to the bottom of the map, so whoever falls in is
// lost. Tops are roughened a little (`rough` 0.7: bark under moss) and capped with moss; rock stays
// smooth. `dress` places decorations into the map's terrain.svg, one rule per slot (`{{name}}`).
//
// This file was laid out from root centerlines (each a stroke with a radius, unioned and traced;
// the east half mirrors the west, all but the trunk) and is the source from here on: edit it by
// hand.
//
// B, a higher lattice: the trunk at the east edge this time, the knee at the west. From each, a
// high root (the shelf, spawns 130 and 1870, and its back, 355 and 1645) over a hollow, and a
// middle root under it (595, 1405) out to a knot on stilts (745, 1255); a thin bridge springs
// between the knots, high over open water. More of the marsh shows under these roots than under
// A's, and the bridge is thin enough to shoot through.
Land(
    size: (2000, 1100),
    islands: [
        // The whole tangle, one landmass: the knee at the west edge, its high and middle
        // roots out to the knot on stilts, the thin bridge, and the same again to the trunk running
        // off the top at the east edge; its feet run off the bottom through the water.
